      "title3_0kgkby7rknxk_html": "Better taste you can trust for 40+ years",
      "headingtext_cvz8v5zrwif_html": "Product Description",
      "textcontent_21o5ex9rkw6j_html": "<ul><li>Refill for our POSTreat Steel Fluoride Removal Cartridge, the world’s first refillable fluoride removal cartridge</li><li>FluoRid is our propriety media, formulated to remove more than 95% of fluoride.<br></li></ul>",
      "textcontent_fcg8fvq2dfd_html": "<ul><li>FluoRid media needs to be replaced every 4 months.</li><li>Our convenient sachets enable you easily to change the FluoRid media in your POSTreat yourself.<br></li><li>By replacing just the media rather than the whole cartridge we save on years worth of discarded material.<br></li></ul><div><br></div>",
      "view_more_text_yqv4owdem4k_html": "View more",
      "view_less_text_yqv4owdem4k_html": "View less",
      "headingtext_037i333bcuod_html": "Better quality you can taste, on tap.",
      "buttoncontent_awcs2j2f8h_html": "Complete Purchase",
      "headingtext_7r1lng6wjij_html": "FAQs",
      "item_title_0_obyhwb3w3en_html": "Is The POSTtreat Compatible With All Gravity Filters Or Just The Phoenix Gravity Filter?",
      "item_title_1_obyhwb3w3en_html": "Can I set it up myself?",
      "item_title_2_obyhwb3w3en_html": "Can I Clean My POSTtreat Fluoride Filter?",
      "textcontent_fxwrc56lf3f_html": "The POSTreat is compatible with all gravity filtration systems. Remember, it can’t be used alone - so you must have a gravity filtration system and existing Carbon Cartridge to use it.<div><br></div>",
      "textcontent_icztbf9rrkg_html": "Absolutely. The POSTtreat is designed for easy DIY set-up with your Phoenix Gravity System. \nYou simply attach your POSTtreat cartridges to the exposed threat of the Carbon Cartridges. We’ll send detailed assembly instructions with your POSTreat filter.<div><div><br></div></div>",
      "textcontent_o41lz187f0t_html": "Yes, it’s simple! You can clean the stainless steel casting of the POSTreat filter - without the FluoRid media inside - in your home using tap water and a soft brush or mild abrasive. The FluoRid media itself will need to be replaced every 4 months. We’ll include detailed instructions when we send it to you.<div><br></div>",
      "headingtext_45y1mu0rgsl_html": "Still have a burning question? See our full FAQs <a href=\"/pages/faq\"><font color=\"#f1d14e\">here.</font></a>",
      "ecomiconlisttitle0_ecom9e4svd9679j_9e4svd9679j_html": "If you don’t like your water filter within 100 days, we’ll give you a full refund.",
      "buttoncontent_ejg46scfpji_html": "Complete Purchase",
      "headingtext_7yt4sozijtk_html": "The Phoenix difference, straight from the source(s)."
    },
